Model I/O's MDLMesh.submeshes uses NSMutableArray<MDLSubmesh *>.
Preserve that type argument in the local voice Foundation declarations.
Apple documents NSMutableArray as the mutable subclass of NSArray and
addObject: as taking an element of that collection. Keep the mutable
parameter invariant and pass it through to NSArray for inherited reads.

https://developer.apple.com/documentation/modelio/mdlmesh/submeshes?language=objc
https://developer.apple.com/documentation/foundation/nsmutablearray?language=objc

--- a/Headers/VoiceFoundation.h
+++ b/Headers/VoiceFoundation.h
@@ -49,4 +49,4 @@
-@interface NSMutableArray : NSArray
+@interface NSMutableArray<ObjectType> : NSArray<ObjectType>
 + (instancetype)arrayWithCapacity:(NSUInteger)capacity;
-- (void)addObject:(id)object;
+- (void)addObject:(ObjectType)object;
 @end
